# RESTful API Architect

## Resource Modeling
- Identify core entities (e.g., `User`, `Video`, `Comment`).
- Define relationships (one-to-many, many-to-many).
- Outline primary use cases: list, create, retrieve, update, delete.
- Reference schema example: [schemas/video.js](mdc:schemas/video.js)

## URL Structure
Use resource-based URLs with proper HTTP verbs:
```
GET    /api/v1/videos              # List videos
POST   /api/v1/videos              # Create video
GET    /api/v1/videos/{id}         # Get video
PUT    /api/v1/videos/{id}         # Full update
PATCH  /api/v1/videos/{id}         # Partial update
DELETE /api/v1/videos/{id}         # Delete video
```
Nest resources and actions when needed:
```
GET    /api/v1/videos/{id}/comments    # Comments for video
POST   /api/v1/videos/{id}/transcode   # Transcode action
```

## Response Format
Standardize all responses:
```json
{
  "data": ...,             // Main payload
  "meta": {               // Pagination or metadata
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 20,
    "total": 100
  },
  "links": {              // HATEOAS links
    "self": "/api/v1/videos?page=1",
    "next": "/api/v1/videos?page=2"
  }
}
```

## Error Format (RFC 7807)
```json
{
  "type": "https://api.example.com/errors/validation",
  "title": "Validation Error",
  "status": 422,
  "detail": "Request contains invalid data",
  "instance": "/api/v1/videos",
  "errors": [
    { "field": "title", "code": "REQUIRED", "message": "Title is required" }
  ]
}
```

## HTTP Status Codes
- `200 OK` for successful GET, PUT, PATCH
- `201 Created` for new resource
- `204 No Content` for successful DELETE
- `400 Bad Request` for malformed requests
- `401 Unauthorized` for missing/invalid auth
- `403 Forbidden` for insufficient permissions
- `404 Not Found` when resource is absent
- `409 Conflict` for resource conflicts
- `422 Unprocessable Entity` for validation errors
- `500 Internal Server Error` for unhandled errors

## Versioning Strategy
- **URL versioning**: e.g., `/api/v1/resources`
- **Header versioning**: client sends `API-Version: 2` header

## Input Validation
Implement robust validation for all incoming requests to ensure data integrity and security.

## Service Layer Pattern
```
src/
├ controllers/    # Handle HTTP requests & responses
├ services/       # Contain business logic & data access
├ models/         # Define data structures/database schemas
└ middleware/     # Handle cross-cutting concerns (e.g., authentication, logging)
```
Example controller: [controllers/videoController.js](mdc:controllers/videoController.js)

## Security and Reliability
- **Rate limiting**: Control access frequency to prevent abuse
- **CORS**: Configure Cross-Origin Resource Sharing policies
- **Authentication**: Implement mechanisms to verify client identity
- **Authorization**: Control access based on user permissions
- **Error handling**: Implement global error handling for consistent responses and logging

## Documentation
Maintain OpenAPI spec:
- File: [openapi.yaml](mdc:openapi.yaml)
- Generate Swagger UI via `swagger-ui-express` or similar tools

## Implementation Checklist
- [ ] Resource URLs follow conventions
- [ ] Status codes used correctly
- [ ] Consistent response & error formats
- [ ] Input validation implemented
- [ ] Authentication & authorization in place
- [ ] Rate limiting configured
- [ ] API versioning implemented
- [ ] API docs updated
- [ ] Logging & monitoring enabled

---
*Always-on guidance for building production-ready RESTful APIs, independent of specific language or framework.*
